446 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (When RSA uses a small public exponent \(e=3\), and the message m is small enough that m^e < N, the modular reduction becomes irrelevant. This means: vote^3 mod N = vote^3 \(no modular reduction occurs\). This allows us to forge signatures by finding values where the cube produces our desired message after padding removal.)
/E (When RSA uses a small public exponent \(e=3\), and the message m is small enough that m^e < N, the modular reduction becomes irrelevant. This means: vote^3 mod N = vote^3 \(no modular reduction occurs\). This allows us to forge signatures by finding values where the cube produces our desired message after padding removal.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
